To determine the volume of water in a rectangular pool that is half full, we first calculate the full volume of the pool using the formula for the volume of a rectangular prism:

$$
\text{Volume} = \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{depth}
$$

Given:
- Length = 12 m
- Width = 6 m
- Depth = 4 m

The full volume of the pool is:

$$
12 \times 6 \times 4 = 288 \, \text{m}^3
$$

Since the pool is half full, we divide the full volume by 2:

$$
\frac{288}{2} = 144 \, \text{m}^3
$$

---

