$ b = \frac{-(-4) \pm \sqrt{(-4)^2 - 4 \times 1 \times (-12)}}{2 \times 1} $

Simplify:

$ b = \frac{4 \pm \sqrt{16 + 48}}{2} $

Because $ (-4)^2 is 16, and 4*1*(-12) is -48, so the discriminant is 16 - 4*(1)*(-12) = 16 + 48 = 64.

